variant, plus t.Parallel on the 7 non-sweep top-level tests. Projected 219-319s and 382-450s. No assertion removed: residue is already asserted directly by before.diff(snapshotState) at commit_atomicity_test.go:178. Out of scope but recorded: the cheap real fix is production-side (hoist namespace validation out of saveJournal or memoize per journal) - routed as a separate story, not smuggled into a test-only rework. Residual risk: parallelizing 88 tests exercises production code concurrently for the first time; a new DATA RACE would be a genuine defect, not a reason to revert. Outcome resource: TASK-260729-3dr6hw_install-race-timeout-diagnosis.md. Logbook entry 2026-07-29 1659.\nagent completed: [analyst] researcher (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260729-6c03cf, pid=78939, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260729-697d2e, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260729-697d2e)\nREVIEW CYCLE 1 — CHANGES REQUESTED to analysis. Preserve the exact timeout inventory, hot-path evidence, 88-test parallelization exclusions, atomicity partition, and assertion map. Required correction: the candidate is already an intentionally dirty delivery worktree, so raw git diff --stat/name-only from HEAD cannot isolate the proposed patch; the 448-file digest covers only the immutable conformance root. Replace it with a pre/post candidate content baseline using verifier3 candidate delta/digests or a task-owned path-sorted SHA-256 manifest, and prove only the literal required test files changed. Exclude unchanged aba_test.go and optional unmeasured atomicity/fixture_test.go from the smallest required patch allowlist. Correct the claim that two algebraically identical install projections are independent and account for full-suite cross-package contention. Evidence: TASK-260729-3dr6hw_review-verdict-cycle-1.md. No Go command or candidate edit was performed.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260729-697d2e, pid=96533, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] researcher (claude) (run=RUN-260729-856b0c, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [analyst] researcher (claude) (run=RUN-260729-856b0c)\nREWORK CYCLE 2 — all five reviewer items addressed; read-only, no Go command executed (a foreign go test -count=1 ./... PID 1686 was live throughout). (1) Candidate-integrity gate rebuilt: git-diff/HEAD checks dropped because the candidate is an intentionally dirty delivery worktree at 17804ce; replaced with a pre/post path-sorted SHA-256 manifest of the worktree (pipefail, real exit) plus a regenerated accepted-worktree rsync delta against .temp/TASK-260729-2kaopg/worktree, gated by a standalone exit-coded script with explicit added/deleted/modified split. (2) Literal runnable commands given for baseline capture, post-patch capture and comparison. The 448-file conformance digest is kept as a separate invariant, not as source integrity. (3) Required allowlist tightened to 13 files; internal/install/aba_test.go and internal/install/atomicity/fixture_test.go are explicitly NOT patch targets. (4) Runtime model rebuilt: the two install projections were one equation rearranged, now labelled a single assumption-based extrapolation; genuinely independent corroboration added from previously unused first-hand gate logs (.temp/TASK-260720-2284br/gates-rework1/gate-race.log real exit 0 with -timeout 45m: internal/install 609.117s vs non-race 228.344s = x2.67; atomicity 1422.407s vs 353.629s = x4.02; focused activation pair x4.27); cross-package contention from the 41-package ./... gate modelled explicitly. Cycle-1 claim that both packages share one race factor is WRONG and corrected — atomicity carries 19-20 journal targets vs install s 8, so more of its wall time sits in the race-instrumented O(P^2) namespace validation. Revised projections: install 890-1000s, atomicity 1284-1494s (cycle 1 s 1121s omitted the three post-sweep tests, which sort after the sweep and were never reached). (5) New corrections found this cycle: TestStrictRegistryPolicyFailsUnknown is registry_e2e_test.go:110, the third declaration in that file, so it is test 73 of 107 and 72 completed before the alarm, not 70/71. Cycle 1 s class-independent-injection-cost inference is now MEASURED from an isolated -v atomicity run (logwork RUN-260729-051449:4697-4765, ok 371.708s): wall reconstruction 22.92+301.67+17.89+18.46+9.97=370.91s of 371.708s, project-hybrid-auto chain alone is 81% of package wall, 7 project injections span 34.99-40.20s and 5 global 23.78-31.27s. That yields the separable phases Patch B needs (project baseline+final 40.74s, mean injection 37.28s) and replaces cycle 1 s single-sample 114s/93s. internal/install/atomicity is NOT in candidate-source-delta-post.txt — byte-identical to the accepted tree — so its race overrun is pre-existing debt masked by -timeout 45m, not a jrrgw9 regression. Patch unchanged in shape: (A) t.Parallel on exactly 88 of 107 internal/install tests, 19 excluded by name (11 t.Setenv, 7 afterDocumentOpen hook users, 1 re-exec child), allowlist verified programmatically as exactly {all 107} minus {the 19}; (B) partition the atomicity sweep to one class per scenario with the full class list retained on the post-sweep coverage assertion, 5 distinct global user homes (globalbins.Select prefers each scenario s own userHome/.local/bin, globalbins.go:146-152), plus t.Parallel on the 7 non-sweep top-level tests. Revised projections 220-340s and 340-460s, both bounded by chain length and by 12 performance cores (cycle 1 divided by 16 logical, counting efficiency cores as equals). Corrected cycle-1 overstatement: the pessimistic 2x concurrency case clears the 600s alarm but NOT the 480s pass bar cycle 1 set itself. One deliberate assertion-strength reduction is named for reviewer sanction: partitioning removes the cross-class residue link (21 ordered class pairs today, none after), with the escalation path if it is refused. Out-of-scope production fix re-recorded: saveJournal validates the namespace graph twice per write across 24 call sites, two inside the 32KiB staging copy loop. Outcome resource updated: TASK-260729-3dr6hw_install-race-timeout-diagnosis.md. Logbook entry 2026-07-29 1732.\nHANDOFF NOTE cycle 2 — checklist items 13/14/15 (Implementation matches AC; Solution fits project architecture; Tests green) are deliberately left UNCHECKED and task-board handoff --role researcher was therefore refused (exit non-zero: unchecked checklist items [13 14 15]). Status was set to to-review explicitly instead. Reason, per the Evidence Honesty Contract: this is a read-only diagnosis task whose scope forbids editing the candidate and forbids running the full/race suite, so item 15 has no green command behind it — no Go test, build or vet command was executed in either cycle, and a foreign go test -count=1 ./... (PID 1686) was live throughout cycle 2. Items 13 and 14 concern an implementation this task does not produce and are the reviewer s independent call, not a self-certification. Checking any of the three would be a false green. The three checks belong to the downstream producer task that applies Patch A and Patch B and runs the focused validation commands in section 7 of the diagnosis. Deliverable: .research/260729_install-race-timeouts.md, SHA-256 198e6f83bce44b21a0706c2d7fa74985e9641b6d3f711c39e5167ffebd17b7de, attached as outcome resource TASK-260729-3dr6hw_install-race-timeout-diagnosis.md.\nagent completed: [analyst] researcher (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260729-856b0c, pid=1265, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260729-b0101b, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260729-b0101b)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260729-b0101b, pid=11068, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] researcher (claude) (run=RUN-260729-6eee2a, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [analyst] researcher (claude) (run=RUN-260729-6eee2a)\nREWORK CYCLE 3 — all four cycle-2 required corrections applied, each independently re-verified against source before editing; read-only, no Go command executed in any cycle of this task. (1) Sec 8.3 rsync expectation fixed: internal/install/cache_conformance_test.go and dryrun_conformance_test.go are candidate-only and already sit in the 23-line delta as *deleting lines, so editing them adds nothing; only the 11 allowlisted files present in both trees can become >fcsT.... entries, giving 34 lines total, not 36. Added an explicit statement that Sec 8.3 structurally CANNOT cover those two files and that the Sec 8.2 pre/post SHA-256 manifest is their only integrity proof, plus a split of the 23 recorded digests into 21 that must stay byte-identical and 2 that MUST change because they are patch targets. (2) saveJournal call sites corrected to 23 — grep -c gives 16 in engine.go (exit 0) and 7 in staging.go (exit 0); cycle 2 wrote 24/8 while listing only seven staging anchors, so the arithmetic was wrong and the anchors were right. Corrected in Sec 2.2 (now a per-file table) and Sec 6; the two copy-loop sites staging.go:141/:161 retained. (3) Patch B1 made implementable: scenario.classes is read at commit_atomicity_test.go:163 (injection loop) AND :206 (full-coverage assertion), so a second field is mandatory. Sec 4.2 now gives literal B1.a-B1.e — add injectClasses []string, leave classes untouched, replace sharedUserHome bool with userHome string, both constructors take injectClass string, and the scenario table is GENERATED by ranging over projectSweepClasses/globalSweepClasses so full class coverage holds structurally rather than by grep. New Sec 4.2.1 is the function-level identifier allowlist (7 entries, nothing else may be introduced); no new imports needed and fixture_test.go stays off the patch list. (4) The blanket no-assertion-removed claim is withdrawn as self-contradictory. New Sec 5.1 treats the cross-class residue chain as INTENTIONALLY RETIRED defence in depth: 31 ordered class pairs (21 project + 10 global) drop to 0; what still proves the property directly is before.diff(snapshotState) at :178 on every injection; what is genuinely lost is a defect that both escapes snapshotState hand-maintained path list AND only manifests through a later class; cycle-2 sanction recorded as attributable; two-class fallback (restores 9 of 31 pairs, ~384s race) named as escalation, not recommendation. Sec 4 preamble and Sec 9 risk 5 restated to match. NEW cycle-3 findings not requested by review: (a) Estimate C downgraded — its non-race denominator 228.344s comes from a 25-line truncated log whose line 21 is FAIL internal/godriver 99.383s (two subtests dying on go-v1 process_timeout, a host-load symptom), and .temp/TASK-260720-2284br/worktree has since been RESET to 4 test files/58 tests with NO atomicity package, so the tree behind x2.67 cannot be re-inspected; patch is now sized against Estimate B (1000s) and Sec 9 risk 2 names this the weakest link. The atomicity x4.02 pair survives because both sides are same-batch and gate-acceptance-verbose.log lets its composition be read directly. (b) New Sec 3.5 adds same-run corroboration of the MECHANISM with no cross-tree assumption: inside the failing gate the three large packages that completed on both sides read x1.45 cmd/curator, x1.39 internal/godriver, x1.25 internal/transaction, while internal/install cannot be under x1.77 — subprocess-dominated packages barely move under -race, in-process O(P^2) namespace validation does. Sub-10s packages excluded as noise. (c) New Sec 4.2.2: Patch B renames sweep subtest paths, and all four accepted filters in gates-cycle5/run-gates.sh:35-41 contain ZERO / characters, so none names a subtest path and none breaks. (d) Stronger safety argument for 5 distinct global user homes — beyond globalbins.Select preferring each own .local/bin (globalbins.go:114, :148-155), the fallback pathDirs scan is gated by safeExistingUserBin -> underHome (:195-196), which rejects a sibling bin outright; two independent mechanisms. (e) Line-number fixes: env.userHome is fixture_test.go:30 not :32, Select is globalbins.go:114 not :113, preferred loop :148-155, entryDigest :226. (f) The 88-name allowlist re-verified programmatically: comm symmetric difference EMPTY in both directions against {all 107} minus {the 19}, all 19 exclusions confirmed to exist; package sizes 107 and 8 match the alarm dumps 0x6b and 0x8. 12 read-only verification commands with real exit codes are tabulated in the cycle-3 rework record. CHECKLIST: item 15 (Tests green) deliberately LEFT UNCHECKED — no Go test, build or vet command was run in any cycle and the task scope forbids running the full/race suite, so checking it would be a false green under the Evidence Honesty Contract; item 15 belongs to the downstream producer task that applies Patch A and Patch B. Items 13/14 checked as producer-side self-assessment: every producer-owned AC clause is satisfied; the AC final clause (reviewer independently checks the plan) is by construction the next cycle gate and is tracked by item 16. Outcome resources: TASK-260729-3dr6hw_install-race-timeout-diagnosis.md updated in place (SHA-256 d2dc2cbc7e332c4590cf49b8b0d37e9753f497b1c177d371554262c73f940b6b) and NEW TASK-260729-3dr6hw_cycle3-rework-record.md. Logbook entry 2026-07-29 1756.\nHANDOFF NOTE cycle 3 — task-board handoff --role researcher was run and REFUSED with real exit 1: "cannot hand off TASK-260729-3dr6hw: unchecked checklist items [15] (Tests green): handoff evidence missing". Status was therefore set to to-review explicitly. Item 15 stays unchecked on purpose: no Go test, build or vet command has been executed in any of the three cycles of this task, and the task scope forbids running the full or race suite, so there is no exit-0 command behind that item and checking it would be a false green under the Evidence Honesty Contract. Item 15 belongs to the downstream producer task that applies Patch A and Patch B and runs the section 7 focused commands. Unlike cycle 2, items 13 and 14 ARE now checked, as the producer-side self-assessment they are — every producer-owned AC clause is satisfied and the AC final clause (reviewer independently checks the plan) is by construction the next cycle gate, tracked by item 16. Reviewer, please verify in this order: (1) that internal/install/cache_conformance_test.go and dryrun_conformance_test.go really are candidate-only, so the corrected 34-line rsync expectation and the statement that only the Sec 8.2 SHA-256 manifest covers them are both right; (2) grep -c saveJournal on internal/transaction/engine.go and staging.go, expecting 16 and 7; (3) that Patch B1 as written in Sec 4.2 compiles conceptually — injectClasses at :163, classes untouched at :206, the generated scenario table, and that the Sec 4.2.1 identifier allowlist is complete; (4) whether the Sec 5.1 framing of the retired cross-class chain is the honest description you asked for, including the named residual exposure and the two-class fallback; (5) the cycle-3 Estimate C downgrade and whether the new Sec 3.5 same-run mechanism corroboration is sound. Deliverable: .research/260729_install-race-timeouts.md, SHA-256 d2dc2cbc7e332c4590cf49b8b0d37e9753f497b1c177d371554262c73f940b6b, attached as outcome resource TASK-260729-3dr6hw_install-race-timeout-diagnosis.md; cycle-3 change record attached as TASK-260729-3dr6hw_cycle3-rework-record.md. No candidate file was modified and no Go command was executed.\nagent completed: [analyst] researcher (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260729-6eee2a, pid=13097, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260729-330d04, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260729-330d04)\nREVIEW CYCLE 3 — CHANGES REQUESTED to analysis. Cycle-2 corrections and the producer plan are independently confirmed. One bounded evidence repair remains in newly added section 3.5: it omits internal/runtimestore (18.630s non-race, 18.244s race, x0.98) while claiming every meaningful completed package is listed, and it incorrectly attributes internal/transaction x1.25 to git/go-build subprocess time despite only two test-binary re-exec sites and no git/go-build test invocation. Correct or remove that causal claim, preserve the accepted plan, and return for review. Evidence: TASK-260729-3dr6hw_review-verdict-cycle-3.md. No candidate edit or Go command was performed.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260729-330d04, pid=19473, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] researcher (claude) (run=RUN-260729-840b17, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [analyst] researcher (claude) (run=RUN-260729-840b17)\nCycle 4 (researcher) — bounded evidence repair of §3.5 per the cycle-3 verdict. Ready for review.\n\nCorrection 1 (selection rule / omitted package): VERIFIED TRUE. internal/runtimestore completed both sides at 18.630s -> 18.244s = x0.98 and was omitted. §3.5 now states a mechanical rule (completed ok on both gates AND max(non-race, race) >= 10s), applied to all 38 both-side-completed packages, yielding exactly 5. All five listed: cmd/curator x1.45, godriver x1.39, transaction x1.25, runtimestore x0.98, managerlock x2.90. The word every is withdrawn and the x1.25-1.45 claim is stated as false. Second omission found and disclosed: managerlock is under 10s non-race but 15.542s under race, so it enters under max() at x2.90 — the largest >10s completed factor and a direct counterexample. Completed range under the rule is x0.98-x2.90; across all 38 it is x0.78 (capabilities) to x8.47 (buildmeta).\n\nCorrection 2 (subprocess attribution): VERIFIED TRUE and the claim is withdrawn entirely for all three packages, not softened for one. internal/transaction has 50 tests, ~33 Prepare sites, exactly 2 exec.Command sites (subprocess_test.go:56,459, both re-executing the test binary) and zero git / go build invocations — an in-process package at x1.25, which refutes cycle 3s in-process => large inflation story. managerlock is also in-process, has zero time.Sleep in tests, and reads x2.90. §3.5 is now explicitly descriptive, carries a static-inventory table with the caveat that call-site counts are not wall-time shares, and takes the reviewers permitted alternative: workload shape via journal target count P (alarm dumps record P=8 for install, P=19/20 for atomicity; transactions Prepare literals hold one to a few targets), labelled a hypothesis predicting direction not magnitude.\n\nCycle-4 findings not requested: (1) atomicitys same-run ratio 603.701/441.122 = x1.37 is censored and lower than cmd/curators x1.45 purely from truncation — now marked as carrying no information, pointing at §3.4s phase-level solve; (2) the same withdrawn causal claim existed in §2.2 and §3.3 closing clauses and was repaired there too, otherwise the §3.5 fix would be cosmetic; (3) §3.1s status row for the mechanism downgraded from measured to hypothesis; (4) new §9 risk 6 records the mechanism as unmeasured and names the cheap confirmation (focused -race -cpuprofile of the atomicity sweep) as outside this tasks no-execution boundary. Old risk 6 renumbered to 7; no cross-reference pointed at it.\n\nPreserved unchanged: §1 timeout inventory, §2.1/§2.3-2.5 hot-path evidence, §4 patch (88/19 Patch A split, Patch B injectClasses selector, generated per-class scenarios, distinct global user homes), §4.0 13-file allowlist with aba_test.go and atomicity/fixture_test.go excluded, §5/§5.1 assertion matrix and retired-invariant disclosure, §7 focused commands and 480s bar, §8 candidate-integrity gates, §6 out-of-scope production finding, and every timing band.\n\nEvidence honesty: no go test/build/vet command was run in any cycle of this task; no candidate file was edited. Two non-zero exits this cycle, both grep zero-match (transaction git/go-build probe, managerlock time.Sleep probe), reported as-is. Checklist item 15 (Tests green) stays UNCHECKED — no green Go command exists behind it and the task forbids running the suite; it belongs to the downstream producer.\n\nDeliverable: .research/260729_install-race-timeouts.md, SHA-256 46316048a5eec0f45c48d34d4dc2751c19a2b7790ddbba1dda85dd0474cf45cb (cycle-3 was d2dc2cbc7e332c4590cf49b8b0d37e9753f497b1c177d371554262c73f940b6b). Board resource updated in place; cycle-4 rework record attached.\nHANDOFF NOTE cycle 4 — task-board handoff --role researcher was run standalone and REFUSED with real exit 1: cannot hand off TASK-260729-3dr6hw: unchecked checklist items [15] (Tests green): handoff evidence missing. Status set to to-review explicitly, same as cycles 2 and 3. Item 15 stays unchecked on purpose: no Go test, build or vet command has been executed in any of the four cycles of this task, the task scope forbids running the full or race suite, and there is no exit-0 command behind that item — checking it would be a false green under the Evidence Honesty Contract. It belongs to the downstream producer task that applies Patch A and Patch B and runs the section 7 focused commands.\n\nReviewer, cycle 4 was a bounded evidence repair only. Please verify in this order:\n(1) The section 3.5 selection rule — completed ok on BOTH verifier-3 gates AND max(non-race, race) >= 10s — really does yield exactly the five listed packages when applied to all 38 both-side-completed packages, and that internal/managerlock (5.366s to 15.542s = x2.90) belongs in the table under max(). It was not named in the cycle-3 verdict; it entered because the corrected rule admits it, and it is the strongest counterexample to the withdrawn homogeneity claim.\n(2) That the subprocess mechanism attribution is withdrawn everywhere, not only in section 3.5: the closing clauses of sections 2.2 and 3.3 and the mechanism row of the section 3.1 status table all carried it and were all repaired.\n(3) That the workload-shape reframing is labelled a hypothesis throughout and that no number in sections 3.2 or 3.4 depends on it — the bands, the 1000s sizing figure, and the atomicity 1284-1494s band are unchanged.\n(4) That marking the atomicity same-run ratio x1.37 as censored and information-free is correct, and that routing the reader to the secti